# Build output and dependencies.
dist/
node_modules/

# Generated, and byte-exact by contract. `fixtures/nft-target/` is produced by
# packages/nft-tracker/scripts/generate-fixtures.mjs and compared byte for byte
# by both codecs; released versions there are frozen under the specification's
# §8.3. Formatting anything in it would rewrite files a test exists to hold
# still. That holds for its Markdown too: `fixtures/nft-target/README.md` stays
# out with the directory.
fixtures/
examples/targets/

# `examples/` is demo pages where the HTML and its inline script are read
# together, so the pages stay out, with the targets, images and videos beside
# them. The modules under `js/` and the tests under `test/` are plain code that
# `npm test` runs, and the README is Markdown like any other: those three are
# checked.
examples/*
!examples/js/
!examples/test/
!examples/README.md

# Out as a whole: the ADRs, whose accepted decisions are never edited in place,
# the specifications, and `docs/benchmarks/`: machine-written measurement data,
# and the record that is cited by line number, so a reformat would move what
# the citations point at.
docs/

# The root README, deliberately (#82). Its wording is the maintainer's
# (AGENTS.md, "Conventions"), and prettier would pad the packages table to the
# width of its longest row, about 1,300 characters, leaving the source
# unreadable while the rendered page is unchanged. It is not frozen with range
# markers instead, because it is edited in the middle, where a range would hide
# every edit from the check. Anchored, so only the root one.
/README.md

# Claude Code's own worktrees, when it makes them inside the checkout. Each is
# a whole second copy of the repository, kept out of git only by
# `.git/info/exclude`, which prettier does not read; without this line
# `"**/*.md"` reaches into them, and `npm run format` rewrites another
# session's files.
.claude/worktrees/
